LOK Calc: an AutoFilter range keeps its rows

Calc regrows an unnamed AutoFilter range from the data around it: each
time the filter list opens (ExtendDataArea, ExtendBackColorArea, so
appended rows join) and whenever a command finds it from a single cell
(ScDocShell::GetDBData, so applying a condition, toggling it off, and
its undo). A totals row right under a marked block joined the filter,
showed in its list and hid with the data; a saved range reopened grew
the same way. Under LOK the range keeps the rows it was set on, as in
Excel, while the cursor is inside it; a cell in another block finds
that block. A single cell still takes the data area when the filter is set.

